that's the interesting thing
about everything being code--

00:41:18.090 --> 00:41:22.502
there's also specific folders to
add plugins for Airflow itself.

00:41:22.502 --> 00:41:24.710
There's questions on whether
we touch the environment

00:41:24.710 --> 00:41:25.820
after it's been created.

00:41:25.820 --> 00:41:27.070
And the answer is no.

00:41:27.070 --> 00:41:30.230
One of the soft spots
on Airflow right now

00:41:30.230 --> 00:41:33.590
is how changes are handled
version to version.

00:41:33.590 --> 00:41:36.080
Right now we think it's
best that we don't change

00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:38.480
your environment's
version or version of any

00:41:38.480 --> 00:41:40.490
of the components
once you deploy it.

00:41:40.490 --> 00:41:43.670
That may change over time
as the Airflow community,

00:41:43.670 --> 00:41:45.890
as Composer matures.

00:41:45.890 --> 00:41:48.200
Will Cloud Composer be
offered in more regions?

00:41:48.200 --> 00:41:49.940
Yes, we are actively
working on it.

00:41:49.940 --> 00:41:51.800
GA is a good example of that.

00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:53.630
Is there a graphical
way to create DAGs?

00:41:53.630 --> 00:41:55.850
Very, very common
question-- the answer is no.

00:41:55.850 --> 00:41:58.640
But this is something of
extreme interest to us and also

00:41:58.640 --> 00:42:00.500
of interest to the
Airflow community.

00:42:00.500 --> 00:42:04.280
So the answer is no,
but I would expect

00:42:04.280 --> 00:42:07.010
that it will happen at
some point in the future.

00:42:07.010 --> 00:42:09.680
Which version of Python
can be used with Composer?

00:42:09.680 --> 00:42:12.590
This is probably the most
Composer-specific question

00:42:12.590 --> 00:42:13.370
that we get.

00:42:13.370 --> 00:42:14.870
Right now it's 2.7.

00:42:14.870 --> 00:42:18.320
We are actively working
on Python 3.5 support.

00:42:18.320 --> 00:42:23.620
You can probably expect that
in a future Composer release.

00:42:23.620 --> 00:42:25.360
Future directions
for Cloud Composer--

00:42:25.360 --> 00:42:27.970
so we showed off
some of the work

00:42:27.970 --> 00:42:29.650
we've done with Kubernetes.

00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:32.260
The intersection of
Kubernetes and Airflow

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:35.200
is exceedingly
interesting to us.

00:42:35.200 --> 00:42:38.860
Google, in terms of the
Composer team and other teams,

00:42:38.860 --> 00:42:42.990
have been involved in work
for Kubernetes and Airflow.

00:42:42.990 --> 00:42:46.040
The KubernetesExecutor is
a good example of that.

00:42:46.040 --> 00:42:49.150
It's not the last example
or the end of the line,

00:42:49.150 --> 00:42:52.570
I think, in terms of
Airflow and Kubernetes.

00:42:52.570 --> 00:42:54.460
We're also working on
additional operators.

00:42:54.460 --> 00:42:57.940
So we want to support
additional API surface area

00:42:57.940 --> 00:43:01.090
coverage of the products that
are already inside of Airflow,

00:43:01.090 --> 00:43:04.210
so things like Dataproc
or BigQuery, data flow.

00:43:04.210 --> 00:43:07.270
We also want to expand support
for new products inside

00:43:07.270 --> 00:43:09.910
of Airflow that
are GCP products.

00:43:09.910 --> 00:43:12.610
Third, resource
usage-- so right now,

00:43:12.610 --> 00:43:16.840
you can create your Composer
environment with a fixed size.

00:43:16.840 --> 00:43:19.430
You can also resize
that environment.

00:43:19.430 --> 00:43:20.890
We're also thinking
of ways that we

00:43:20.890 --> 00:43:23.770
can increase the elasticity
of that environment,

00:43:23.770 --> 00:43:27.970
based on workflows that are
executing on that environment.

00:43:27.970 --> 00:43:29.740
Much like a lot of
our managed services,

00:43:29.740 --> 00:43:32.350
we want to tightly
constrain the resources

00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:33.970
that you're using
for an environment

00:43:33.970 --> 00:43:37.270
to what's actually going
on in that environment.

00:43:37.270 --> 00:43:38.680
There's a ton of
different things

00:43:38.680 --> 00:43:43.210
that you can do to get involved
with either Airflow, if you

00:43:43.210 --> 00:43:47.820
don't like Composer, and that's
totally OK, or Composer itself.

00:43:47.820 --> 00:43:51.310
Airflow, the Apache website for
Airflow's a really good place

00:43:51.310 --> 00:43:51.980
to get started.

00:43:51.980 --> 00:43:53.847
There's links to
the mailing list.

00:43:53.847 --> 00:43:55.430
They have pretty
active mailing lists.

00:43:55.430 --> 00:43:57.221
There's a lot of
information for how to get

00:43:57.221 --> 00:43:58.570
involved in that community.

00:43:58.570 --> 00:44:01.630
In terms of Composer, we
have our documentation

00:44:01.630 --> 00:44:02.740
for the product.

00:44:02.740 --> 00:44:07.120
There's also a Google group
mailing list that you can join.

00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:09.880
Please ask questions
on that mailing list.

00:44:09.880 --> 00:44:13.640
There's also a Stack Overflow
tag that we look at as a team.

00:44:13.640 --> 00:44:17.050
So if you have Composer-specific
questions, please use that tag.

00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:19.840
Because the more questions
that you ask with that tag,

00:44:19.840 --> 00:44:22.314
the less likely it is that
other people will need to hunt

00:44:22.314 --> 00:44:23.980
and peck for that
information over time.

00:44:23.980 --> 00:44:26.229
And we just can't anticipate
all of the questions that

00:44:26.229 --> 00:44:28.750
might come up over time.

00:44:28.750 --> 00:44:30.640
As a plug, there
is a Meetup group,

00:44:30.640 --> 00:44:34.850
if you happen to be local
to the Bay area for Airflow.

00:44:34.850 --> 00:44:37.150
There is going to be an
event in September, which

00:44:37.150 --> 00:44:39.970
is going to be hosted by
the Cloud Composer team

00:44:39.970 --> 00:44:41.760
at the Google Sunnyvale office.

00:44:41.760 --> 00:44:44.260
So if you are local,
please sign up.

00:44:44.260 --> 00:44:49.510
We just put up the
Meetup event for that.

00:44:49.510 --> 00:44:52.540
So it's something to check
out if you're curious.

00:44:52.540 --> 00:44:54.650
With that, thank you all
very much for being here.

00:44:54.650 --> 00:44:56.230
We sincerely appreciate it.

00:44:56.230 --> 00:44:59.950
And again, thank you to everyone
who used Composer and gave us

00:44:59.950 --> 00:45:00.901
feedback.

00:45:00.901 --> 00:45:01.900
We're open to questions.

00:45:01.900 --> 00:45:03.639
We have five minutes.

00:45:03.639 --> 00:45:05.680
If you have questions,
please come up to the mic.

00:45:05.680 --> 00:45:07.570
Happy to answer any
questions you guys have.

00:45:07.570 --> 00:45:08.070
[APPLAUSE]

00:45:08.070 --> 00:45:10.620
[LOGO MUSIC PLAYING]

